import{_ as t,o as a,c as s,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CyZTVJbV.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"announcements/v1.27/x-thread-en.md","filePath":"announcements/v1.27/x-thread-en.md"}'),r={name:"announcements/v1.27/x-thread-en.md"};function i(n,e,d,c,l,p){return a(),s("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<p>1/ kiwa v1.27 is out — Mutation testing sweep milestone. After v1.11 landed <code>@kiwa/quality-metrics</code> v0.1 with <code>mutationFromCounts</code> + a fixed 60 % kill-rate axis on the 11-axis release gate, v1.27 stacks <strong>4-tier mutation threshold SSOT + Stryker rollout across all 33 kiwa packages + a 12-axis release gate with <code>mutation.tier</code> as the new axis</strong>. <code>@kiwa/quality-metrics</code> v0.2.0 → v0.3.0 minor bump. 5 new primitives + 20 snippet tests + 6 sub-Issue merges.</p><p>2/ Why 4 tiers? A single universal floor has 3 failure modes — threshold drift (<code>Core</code> packages naturally test higher than SaaS mocks, one number cannot describe both), kill-rate formula drift (Stryker exposes 4 different numbers, teams silently pick the one that flatters), regression detection drift (rebuilding the baseline hides regressions). The 4-rule SSOT (<code>docs/concepts/mutation-testing-ssot.md</code>) — kill-rate formula pinned at <code>killed / (killed + survived + timeout + error)</code> / 4-tier floor pinned by code shape (Core 80 / Framework 70 / SaaS 65 / Test type 60) / baseline JSON persisted at <code>.mutation-baseline/{package}.json</code> / tier-aware 12-axis gate — is the smallest set that makes kiwa mutation suites comparable across packages, milestones, and forks.</p><p>3/ v1.27-1 Stryker infra 基盤 (Issue #957) — 34-package <code>stryker.config.mjs</code> land + <code>test:mutation</code> script + <code>.stryker-tmp/</code> gitignore + <code>.mutation-baseline/{package}.json</code> persistence. 4-tier threshold rationale SSOT lives at <code>docs/quality/mutation-thresholds.md</code>, and every downstream <code>stryker.config.mjs</code> reads its thresholds from <code>resolveMutationTier</code> — no per-package override.</p><p>4/ v1.27-2 core + framework layer mutation sweep (Issue #963) — 9 core-layer packages (core / dapp / api / ui / data / cli-test / observability / e2e / cli) + 11 framework-adapter packages (a11y / visual / nextjs / nuxt / sveltekit / remix / astro / solidstart / qwikcity / edge / fresh / hono / solidjs). 3-layer harness (source + test + mutant) SSOT + parallel Stryker run across 20 packages with tier-aware gates.</p><p>5/ v1.27-3 test type + SaaS layer mutation sweep (Issue #966) — 3 test-type packages (a11y / visual / component) + 10 SaaS-layer packages (auth / queue / cache / orm / payment / streaming / search / mcp / agent / realtime). Provider-specific baseline patterns kept in the same <code>.mutation-baseline/{package}.json</code> shape so <code>PACKAGE_TIER</code> map stays single-file.</p><p>6/ v1.27-4 release gate 12-axis 拡張 (Issue #959) — <code>evaluateReleaseGate(report, thresholdOverrides, { mutationTier })</code> opts a report into a 12th axis (<code>mutation.tier</code>) that fails when kill-rate drops below the tier floor. Existing 7 / 11 axis callers stay unchanged when <code>mutationTier</code> is omitted. <code>MutationTierBelowFloor</code> error carries the offending tier + package + rate + floor.</p><p>7/ v1.27-5 docs (Issue #968) — tutorial 50 (Stryker + kill-rate baseline + tier gate walkthrough) + tutorial 51 (22 → 33 package sweep methodology) + concept doc <code>mutation-testing-ssot.md</code> 4-rule SSOT + migration <code>v1.26 → v1.27</code> (additive-only) + snippet validation <code>docs-tutorial-v1.27.test.ts</code> (20 test) re-runs every code snippet against the real <code>@kiwa/quality-metrics</code> v0.3 API.</p><p>8/ v1.27-6 publish (Issue #961) — <code>@kiwa/quality-metrics</code> v0.2.0 → v0.3.0 minor bump goes to npm. plugin.json 1.27.0 + new mutation-focused keywords + Roadmap ✅ v1.27 row + announcement 4 file + release-smoke <code>v1-27-publish.test.ts</code> (7 axis invariant) + docs-e2e <code>V1_27_PAGES</code> (5 pages) + <strong>release script filter fix</strong> — <code>@kiwa/quality-metrics</code> added to both <code>-F</code> and <code>--filter</code> halves (v1.14 payment + v1.25 perf-harness lesson, 3rd application of the pattern). gh-pages published via <code>/docs-publish-kiwa</code>.</p><p>9/ 17-milestone streak — v1.11 (release gate) → v1.12 (non-determinism) → v1.13 (time-axis) → v1.14 (horizontal expansion) → v1.15 (AI-LLM depth) → v1.16 (component depth) → v1.17 (Observability v2) → v1.18 (Blockchain depth) → v1.19 (Framework depth) → v1.20 (Streaming depth) → v1.21 (Auth depth) → v1.22 (Auth depth II) → v1.23 (Payment depth) → v1.24 (Edge / Serverless depth) → v1.25 (Perf-harness sweep) → v1.26 (Database depth) → v1.27 (Mutation testing sweep). Every milestone since v1.11 has landed 6 sub-Issues in full. Roadmap: <a href="https://github.com/cardene777/kiwa#roadmap" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://github.com/cardene777/kiwa#roadmap</a></p>',9)])])}const h=t(r,[["render",i]]);export{u as __pageData,h as default};
